SIM-21: keep a GPV's curve index in one place, Link.Kc

The curve index of a GPV was held in Link.Kc (what EN_GPV_CURVE and
EN_deletecurve update), Link.InitSetting (copied into LinkSetting, which
gpvcoeff() read) and Control.Setting (copied into LinkSetting when a
control fired). Deleting another curve or assigning a new one left the
solver on a different curve from the one reported. Make gpvcoeff() read
Kc; keep InitSetting (what saveinpfile writes) equal to Kc in
adjustcurves() and EN_setlinkvalue, also while the solver is open; and
stop controls from writing a curve index into a GPV's setting.

Deleting a GPV's own curve now leaves it with no curve, which CRASH-16
reports at EN_openH. While the solver is open, EN_GPV_CURVE refuses
curve 0 with error 206, since the solver reads Kc directly.

Requires: CRASH-16 SIM-19

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-16
and SIM-19:
    git apply CRASH-16_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-19_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-21_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 001b3d1..61dc837 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -4354,8 +4354,11 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinkvalue(EN_Project p, int index, int property, double valu
         {
             curveIndex = ROUND(value);
             if (curveIndex < 0 || curveIndex > net->Ncurves) return 206;
+            // The solver uses Kc, so it must stay a valid curve while open
+            if (curveIndex == 0 && hyd->OpenHflag) return 206;
             Link[index].Kc = curveIndex;
-            if (hyd->OpenHflag == FALSE) Link[index].InitSetting = curveIndex;
+            Link[index].InitSetting = curveIndex;
+            if (hyd->OpenHflag) hyd->LinkSetting[index] = curveIndex;
             if (curveIndex > 0) net->Curve[curveIndex].Type = HLOSS_CURVE;
         }
         break;
diff --git a/src/hydcoeffs.c b/src/hydcoeffs.c
index d0b03c2..10066dc 100644
--- a/src/hydcoeffs.c
+++ b/src/hydcoeffs.c
@@ -970,11 +970,11 @@ void  gpvcoeff(Project *pr, int k)
 
     // Otherwise utilize segment of head loss curve
     // bracketing current flow (curve index is stored
-    // in valve's setting)
+    // in valve's Kc property)
     else
     {
         // Index of valve's head loss curve
-        i = (int)ROUND(hyd->LinkSetting[k]);
+        i = (int)ROUND(pr->network.Link[k].Kc);
 
         // Adjusted flow rate
         q = ABS(hyd->LinkFlow[k]);
diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..3c78fec 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -625,7 +625,8 @@ int  controls(Project *pr)
             s2 = control->Status;
             k1 = hyd->LinkSetting[k];
             k2 = k1;
-            if (link->Type > PIPE) k2 = control->Setting;
+            // (a GPV control only changes status; its curve index is in Kc)
+            if (link->Type > PIPE && link->Type != GPV) k2 = control->Setting;
 
             // Check if a re-opened pump needs its flow reset
             if (link->Type == PUMP && s1 == CLOSED && s2 == OPEN)
diff --git a/src/project.c b/src/project.c
index 9d7c7f1..195bb3f 100644
--- a/src/project.c
+++ b/src/project.c
@@ -1255,6 +1255,7 @@ void adjustcurves(Network *network, int index)
             curve = INT(network->Link[k].Kc);
             adjustcurve(&curve, index);
             network->Link[k].Kc = curve;
+            network->Link[k].InitSetting = curve;
         }
     }
 }
